<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Social Security Act 1938</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1938</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Social Security Act 1938 was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a> law passed by the first Labour government under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/michael-joseph-savage">Michael Joseph Savage</a>. It created a comprehensive system of state support, including old-age, invalid and widows' benefits, family allowances and free hospital treatment, funded by a special tax. It is regarded as the foundation of the New Zealand welfare state.</p></div>
